{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "promiseunlocked-api-collection",
    "name": "PromiseUnlocked API",
    "description": "Postman notes:\n1. Run `Login` first to store `bearerToken`.\n2. Requests that use `{{participantId}}`, `{{sessionId}}`, or `{{interactionId}}` depend on a previous list request.\n3. The list requests automatically save a random id from the response into the matching environment variable so the next request can reuse it.\n4. For participant self-serve flows, `List Participants` returns only the authenticated participant unless the token belongs to an admin.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Login",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"test@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "// Save idToken as Bearer token",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  var data = pm.response.json();",
              "  if (data.idToken) {",
              "    pm.environment.set('bearerToken', data.idToken);",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "List Participants",
      "request": {
        "description": "Dependency note: run this before `Get Participant`, `List Sessions for Participant`, `Get Session`, `List Interactions for Session`, or `Get Interaction`. On success, a random `participantId` from the response is stored in the environment.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/participants",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "participants"]
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "// Save a random participantId for the next dependent requests.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  var data = pm.response.json();",
              "  var participants = Array.isArray(data.participants) ? data.participants.filter(function (participant) {",
              "    return participant && participant.uid;",
              "  }) : [];",
              "  if (participants.length > 0) {",
              "    var randomParticipant = participants[Math.floor(Math.random() * participants.length)];",
              "    pm.environment.set('participantId', randomParticipant.uid);",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get My Participant Profile",
      "request": {
        "description": "Authenticated participant route. Use this for the signed-in user's own participant profile. On success, the returned `participant.uid` is saved as `participantId` so later participant/session requests can reuse it.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/participants/me",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "participants", "me"]
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "// Save the authenticated participantId for later dependent requests.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  var data = pm.response.json();",
              "  if (data.participant && data.participant.uid) {",
              "    pm.environment.set('participantId', data.participant.uid);",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "List My Sessions",
      "request": {
        "description": "Authenticated participant route. Lists only the signed-in user's sessions. On success, a random `sessionId` is saved for the next dependent request.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/participants/me/sessions",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "participants", "me", "sessions"]
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "// Save a random sessionId for the next dependent requests.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  var data = pm.response.json();",
              "  var sessions = Array.isArray(data.sessions) ? data.sessions.filter(function (session) {",
              "    return session && session.id;",
              "  }) : [];",
              "  if (sessions.length > 0) {",
              "    var randomSession = sessions[Math.floor(Math.random() * sessions.length)];",
              "    pm.environment.set('sessionId', randomSession.id);",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get My Session",
      "request": {
        "description": "Authenticated participant route. Requires `sessionId`. Run `List My Sessions` first so the environment variable is set automatically.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/participants/me/sessions/{{sessionId}}",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "participants", "me", "sessions", "{{sessionId}}"]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Get Participant",
      "request": {
        "description": "Dependency note: requires `participantId`. Run `List Participants` first so the environment variable is set automatically.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/participants/{{participantId}}",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "participants", "{{participantId}}"]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "List Sessions for Participant",
      "request": {
        "description": "Dependency note: requires `participantId` from `List Participants`. On success, a random `sessionId` from the response is stored in the environment for the next dependent requests.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/participants/{{participantId}}/sessions",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "participants", "{{participantId}}", "sessions"]
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "// Save a random sessionId for the next dependent requests.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  var data = pm.response.json();",
              "  var sessions = Array.isArray(data.sessions) ? data.sessions.filter(function (session) {",
              "    return session && session.id;",
              "  }) : [];",
              "  if (sessions.length > 0) {",
              "    var randomSession = sessions[Math.floor(Math.random() * sessions.length)];",
              "    pm.environment.set('sessionId', randomSession.id);",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get Session",
      "request": {
        "description": "Dependency note: requires both `participantId` and `sessionId`. Run `List Participants` and then `List Sessions for Participant` first.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/participants/{{participantId}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "participants", "{{participantId}}", "sessions", "{{sessionId}}"]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "List Interactions for Session",
      "request": {
        "description": "Returns the interaction documents for a session ordered by timestamp ascending. Optional query param: limit.\nDependency note: requires `participantId` and `sessionId`. Run `List Participants` and `List Sessions for Participant` first. On success, a random `interactionId` from the response is stored in the environment.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/participants/{{participantId}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/interactions?limit=50",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "participants",
            "{{participantId}}",
            "sessions",
            "{{sessionId}}",
            "interactions"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "50",
              "description": "Optional. Max 200."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": [
        {
          "name": "200 OK",
          "originalRequest": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/participants/{{participantId}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/interactions?limit=50",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "participants",
                "{{participantId}}",
                "sessions",
                "{{sessionId}}",
                "interactions"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "50"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "status": "OK",
          "code": 200,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "body": "{\n  \"interactions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"abc123\",\n      \"sequenceIndex\": 1,\n      \"question\": \"Tell me about a time you solved a hard problem?\",\n      \"answer\": \"I debugged a production issue by tracing logs and isolating the failing service.\",\n      \"inputMethod\": \"text\",\n      \"mappingOutcome\": \"mapped\",\n      \"mappedCategory\": \"Problem-Solving & Systems Thinking\",\n      \"isWeakFit\": false,\n      \"isAlreadyMapped\": false,\n      \"justification\": \"The answer shows structured analysis and resolution of a complex issue.\",\n      \"matchedToCategory\": null,\n      \"matchedToSequenceIndex\": null,\n      \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-03T15:22:11.000Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
        }
      ],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "// Save a random interactionId for the next dependent request.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  var data = pm.response.json();",
              "  var interactions = Array.isArray(data.interactions) ? data.interactions.filter(function (interaction) {",
              "    return interaction && interaction.id;",
              "  }) : [];",
              "  if (interactions.length > 0) {",
              "    var randomInteraction = interactions[Math.floor(Math.random() * interactions.length)];",
              "    pm.environment.set('interactionId', randomInteraction.id);",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get Interaction",
      "request": {
        "description": "Returns a single interaction document for the session.\nDependency note: requires `participantId`, `sessionId`, and `interactionId`. Run the list requests first so Postman sets those environment variables automatically.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/participants/{{participantId}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/interactions/{{interactionId}}",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "participants",
            "{{participantId}}",
            "sessions",
            "{{sessionId}}",
            "interactions",
            "{{interactionId}}"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": [
        {
          "name": "200 OK",
          "originalRequest": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/participants/{{participantId}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/interactions/{{interactionId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "participants",
                "{{participantId}}",
                "sessions",
                "{{sessionId}}",
                "interactions",
                "{{interactionId}}"
              ]
            }
          },
          "status": "OK",
          "code": 200,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "body": "{\n  \"interaction\": {\n    \"id\": \"abc123\",\n    \"sequenceIndex\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Tell me about a time you solved a hard problem?\",\n    \"answer\": \"I debugged a production issue by tracing logs and isolating the failing service.\",\n    \"inputMethod\": \"text\",\n    \"mappingOutcome\": \"mapped\",\n    \"mappedCategory\": \"Problem-Solving & Systems Thinking\",\n    \"isWeakFit\": false,\n    \"isAlreadyMapped\": false,\n    \"justification\": \"The answer shows structured analysis and resolution of a complex issue.\",\n    \"matchedToCategory\": null,\n    \"matchedToSequenceIndex\": null,\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-03T15:22:11.000Z\"\n  }\n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Notes - Skills, Stamps, Awarded",
      "request": {
        "description": "Backend status note: there are currently no Express API routes in `backend/src` for authenticated `me` skills, stamps, awarded items, or dedicated `me` interactions. The available self-service routes today are `/api/participants/me`, `/api/participants/me/sessions`, and `/api/participants/me/sessions/:sessionId`. For interactions, use the existing participant/session route after `Get My Participant Profile` sets `participantId`."
      },
      "response": []
    }
  ],
  "event": [],
  "variable": [{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000" }]
}
